#ident	"@(#)gen++:d.pkg/rc/README	1.6"
This directory contains all that is needed to build the OO Rule Checker.
These rules are taken from "OO Programming Rules and Guidelines, Version 3"
by Logothetis and Wilkinson.  A postscript version of this memo is included
in docs/*.ps.

To build, you must first edit makefile to set macros
	GEN = gen++ installation directory
	CPL = C++ compiler, version 3.0.*
	CC  = C compiler
edit 'mk' to set the path for the license file, then type
	mk
The makefile will build
	analyzer
which implements the rule checker.
To use this analyzer, edit Checker to set
	CC = 3.0.* C++ compiler
	TOOLSDIR = directory containing rule checker
	GENPP_LICENSE_FILE
and copy Checker to your favorite bin.

Checker will take the same command line as CC.  For each file x.c, output
will be written to x.OO.
For example, to run the rule checker on a C++ source file, type
	Checker [preprocessor options] file.c
The file 'file.OO' will then contain the diagnostics generated
by the rule checker.
